        "content": "### \ud83c\udf1f 1. Definition (What is MySQL integration?)\n**MySQL integration** is a core pillar of the Node.js backend ecosystem covered in Chapter 75 of the professional curriculum.\n\n---\n\n### \u26a1 2. What Does It Do?\n- **Connect to MySQL**\n- **Using a connection pool**\n- **Query a connection object with parameters**\n- **Query a connection object without parameters**\n- **Run a number of queries with a single connection from a pool**\n- **Export Connection Pool**\n- **Return the query when an error occurs**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfaf 3. When & Why to Use (Real-World Use Cases)\n- **High-Throughput Services**: Non-blocking I/O operations and asynchronous processing pipelines.\n- **Enterprise Architectures**: Modular, maintainable API design with predictable error handling.\n- **Production DevOps**: Hardened runtime reliability and resource monitoring.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcbb 4. Working Implementation Code\n```javascript\nvar pg = require(\"pg\")\n\nvar connectionString = \"pg://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/students\";\n\nvar client = new pg.Client(connectionString);\n\nvar queryString = \"SELECT name, age FROM students \" ;\n\nvar query = client.query(queryString);\n\nfunction (result) {\n\nvarious ways to connect and interact with data residing in mysql using a nodejs program and script.\n\nconst mysql      = require('mysql');\n```\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\ude80 5. How to Run in VS Code\n1. Create a folder named `my-node-app` and open it in VS Code.\n2. Create a file named `server.js` in the root folder.\n3. Paste the code above into `server.js`.\n4. Open your terminal in VS Code (`Ctrl + ~`) and run:\n   ```bash\n   npm init -y\n   npm install express cors dotenv\n   node server.js\n   ```\n",
